WEBVTT

00:00:18.608 --> 00:00:20.627
Dad's missing I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:21.855
I can't do this alone.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.296
Dad's giving us a job to do.

00:00:23.331 --> 00:00:25.321
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:25.356 --> 00:00:27.277
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:27.312 --> 00:00:30.270
This Demon killed mom and
Jess. I got to find dad.

00:00:30.305 --> 00:00:32.018
I've got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:32.851
I'm Meg.

00:00:32.886 --> 00:00:33.878
So, where are you headed?

00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:34.870
No way I'm telling you.

00:00:34.871 --> 00:00:37.235
You could be some freak.

00:00:37.782 --> 00:00:39.055
Dad.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.014
<i>ust to get a glimpse
beyond this illusion</i>

00:00:43.049 --> 00:00:44.231
<i>I was soaring ever</i>

00:00:44.266 --> 00:00:47.107
1835, Samuel Colt made a special gun.

00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:49.948
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:50.986 --> 00:00:54.672
<i>Though my eyes could see
I still was a blind man</i>

00:00:54.707 --> 00:00:58.358
<i>Though my mind could
think I still was a mad man</i>

00:00:58.393 --> 00:01:01.131
<i>I hear the voices when I'm dreaming</i>

00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:04.494
I have nightmares. And
sometime they come true.

00:01:06.356 --> 00:01:09.752
<i>Carry on my wayward son</i>

00:01:09.787 --> 00:01:11.747
<i>There'll be peace when you are</i>

00:01:11.782 --> 00:01:14.918
You two are all I've got. But I
guess we are stronger as a family.

00:01:14.953 --> 00:01:16.892
We go after this thing, together.

00:01:16.927 --> 00:01:17.395
Yes, sir.

00:01:17.396 --> 00:01:19.953
<i>Don't you cry no more</i>

00:01:44.891 --> 00:01:46.170
Good morning.

00:01:46.861 --> 00:01:48.524
Can I help you?

00:01:49.663 --> 00:01:51.640
I kind of...

00:01:51.675 --> 00:01:53.617
I need to talk.

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:57.613
That's what I'm here for.

00:02:00.059 --> 00:02:02.681
I've done some things.

00:02:03.914 --> 00:02:05.580
Not good things.

00:02:05.615 --> 00:02:08.419
Well, there's always
forgiveness for us who seek it.

00:02:08.454 --> 00:02:10.601
For everyone?

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.911
Are you sure?

00:02:12.946 --> 00:02:14.659
I'll like to say...

00:02:14.694 --> 00:02:18.161
Salvation was created for sinners.

00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:22.652
Tell me what's on your mind.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:27.331
Well, I've lied a lot.

00:02:27.366 --> 00:02:29.406
I've Stolen.

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:31.411
I've lusted...

00:02:31.446 --> 00:02:34.251
And the other day I met this man.

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:37.994
A nice guy, you know?

00:02:38.715 --> 00:02:44.698
We had a really good
chat. Sort of like this.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:51.487
And I slit his throat and ripped
his heart out through his chest.

00:02:51.522 --> 00:02:53.531
Does that make me a bad person?

00:02:53.566 --> 00:02:55.087
I know what you are.

00:02:57.215 --> 00:02:59.518
You can't be here.

00:02:59.553 --> 00:03:01.275
This is hollowed ground.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.784
Please...

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:05.971
Maybe that works in the minor leagues.

00:03:06.006 --> 00:03:08.649
But not with me.

00:03:33.307 --> 00:03:35.905
You throw like a girl.

00:03:36.728 --> 00:03:38.948
What do you want?

00:03:39.396 --> 00:03:42.075
The Winchesters.

00:03:42.242 --> 00:03:45.681
I haven't spoken to John
Winchester for over a year.

00:03:45.716 --> 00:03:47.725
You're wasting you time.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.778
Even if I knew where they were

00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:52.197
I'd never tell you.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.322
I know.

00:04:45.027 --> 00:04:46.584
So, this is it?

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.887
This is everything I know.

00:04:48.922 --> 00:04:51.819
Look, our whole lives we've been
searching for this demon right?

00:04:51.854 --> 00:04:54.212
Not a trace. Just nothing.

00:04:54.247 --> 00:04:56.536
Until about a year ago.

00:04:56.571 --> 00:04:58.702
For the first time I picked up a trail.

00:04:58.737 --> 00:04:59.899
That's when you took off.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:00.836
Yeah.

00:05:00.871 --> 00:05:04.604
The demon must have come
out of hiding or hibernation.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.817
All right, so what's
this trail you've found?

00:05:06.852 --> 00:05:10.317
Starts in Arizona. Then
New Jersey, California.

00:05:10.352 --> 00:05:12.673
House is burned down to the ground.

00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:15.360
It's going after families.

00:05:15.395 --> 00:05:16.946
Just like it went after us.

00:05:16.981 --> 00:05:18.365
Families with infants?

00:05:18.366 --> 00:05:19.386
Yeah.

00:05:19.421 --> 00:05:22.470
The night of the kid's
six month birthday.

00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:24.575
I was six months old that night?

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:26.215
Exactly six months.

00:05:26.269 --> 00:05:31.666
So, basically this demon is going
after these kids for some reason.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:35.102
Same way it came for me.

00:05:35.847 --> 00:05:38.837
So, mom's death?

00:05:39.124 --> 00:05:40.690
Jessica, it's all because of me?

00:05:40.725 --> 00:05:41.592
We don't know that Sam.

00:05:41.593 --> 00:05:43.205
Oh, really? Cause I say
we're pretty damn sure Dean.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.663
For the last time. What happened
to them is not your fault.

00:05:45.698 --> 00:05:48.087
Yeah, you're right. It's not
my fault. But it's my problem.

00:05:48.122 --> 00:05:50.087
No, it's not your
problem. It's our problem.

00:05:50.122 --> 00:05:54.158
Okay. That's enough.

00:05:59.318 --> 00:06:01.112
So, why is it doing it?

00:06:01.147 --> 00:06:02.198
What does it want?

00:06:02.233 --> 00:06:04.951
I wish I had more answers. I do.

00:06:04.986 --> 00:06:07.635
I've always been one step behind it.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:11.310
Look I've never got
there in time to save...

00:06:16.498 --> 00:06:19.729
So how do we find it?
Before it hits again?

00:06:19.929 --> 00:06:21.897
There' re signs.

00:06:21.932 --> 00:06:23.464
Look, it took me a
while to see the patterns

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:28.385
but days before these fires
signs crop up in an area.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:33.272
Cattle deaths, temperature
fluctuations, electrical storms.

00:06:33.827 --> 00:06:36.831
And then we backed and checked...

00:06:36.866 --> 00:06:40.137
These things happened in Lawrence?

00:06:40.172 --> 00:06:43.408
A week before your mother died.

00:06:45.291 --> 00:06:48.237
And in Palo Alto.

00:06:50.131 --> 00:06:52.558
Before Jessica.

00:06:52.593 --> 00:06:56.952
And these signs they're starting again.

00:06:57.336 --> 00:06:59.444
Where?

00:06:59.582 --> 00:07:02.575
Salvation, Iowa.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:35.635
Damn it!

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.666
What is it?

00:07:36.701 --> 00:07:37.821
Son of a bitch!

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:38.942
What is it?

00:07:39.395 --> 00:07:40.926
I just got a call from Caleb.

00:07:40.961 --> 00:07:42.212
Is he okay?

00:07:42.247 --> 00:07:45.448
He's fine. Jim Murphy's dead.

00:07:45.483 --> 00:07:47.541
Pastor Jim?

00:07:48.592 --> 00:07:50.593
How?

00:07:50.628 --> 00:07:52.692
Throat was slashed.

00:07:52.727 --> 00:07:55.407
He bled out.

00:07:58.239 --> 00:08:01.259
Caleb said they found traces
of sulfur at Jim's place.

00:08:01.294 --> 00:08:02.870
The Demon?

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.221
The Demon?

00:08:05.256 --> 00:08:08.228
I don't know. Could be. He just got...

00:08:08.263 --> 00:08:11.325
He got careless he slipped up.

00:08:12.118 --> 00:08:15.537
Maybe the Demon knows
we're getting close.

00:08:15.572 --> 00:08:16.768
What do you want to do?

00:08:16.803 --> 00:08:19.136
Now we act like every second counts.

00:08:19.171 --> 00:08:22.245
There's two hospitals and a
health center in this County.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:24.303
We split up, we cover more ground.

00:08:24.338 --> 00:08:25.673
I want records.

00:08:25.708 --> 00:08:29.775
I want a list of every infant who's
gonna be six months old in the next week.

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.771
Dad, that can be dozens of kids.

00:08:31.806 --> 00:08:33.660
How the hell are we gonna
know which one's the right one?

00:08:33.695 --> 00:08:36.301
We check them all. That's how.

00:08:36.793 --> 00:08:39.548
You got any better ideas?

00:08:41.072 --> 00:08:43.002
No, sir.

00:08:51.772 --> 00:08:53.189
Dad?

00:08:56.314 --> 00:08:58.373
Yeah.

00:08:59.917 --> 00:09:01.989
It's Jim.

00:09:02.363 --> 00:09:04.656
You know, I can't...

00:09:10.724 --> 00:09:12.888
This ends, now.

00:09:12.923 --> 00:09:15.017
I'm ending it.

00:09:15.052 --> 00:09:18.052
I don't care what it takes.

00:10:07.743 --> 00:10:08.954
Here you go, officer.

00:10:08.989 --> 00:10:10.103
Thank you.

00:10:26.207 --> 00:10:29.325
Hi, is there anything I can do for you?

00:10:29.684 --> 00:10:32.050
Oh, God, yes.

00:10:33.734 --> 00:10:36.342
Only I uh...

00:10:36.377 --> 00:10:39.294
Working right now, so...

00:11:29.487 --> 00:11:31.614
Train.

00:12:40.142 --> 00:12:41.425
Hi.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:45.265
Here, let me hold that. I don't
think you need that anymore.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.916
She's gorgeous, is she yours?

00:12:47.951 --> 00:12:48.583
Yeah.

00:12:48.618 --> 00:12:50.113
Oh, wow. Hi.

00:12:50.114 --> 00:12:53.082
I'm sorry, I'm Sam. I
just moved in up the block.

00:12:53.117 --> 00:12:54.541
Oh, hey. I'm Monica.

00:12:54.576 --> 00:12:55.010
Monica.

00:12:55.011 --> 00:12:55.934
This is Rosy.

00:12:55.969 --> 00:12:56.527
Rosy?

00:12:56.528 --> 00:12:58.952
Yeah. So, welcome to the neighborhood.

00:12:58.987 --> 00:13:00.492
Thank you.

00:13:00.527 --> 00:13:02.050
She's such a good baby.

00:13:02.085 --> 00:13:04.239
I know, she... I mean, she never cries.

00:13:04.274 --> 00:13:06.447
She just stares at everybody.

00:13:06.482 --> 00:13:08.586
Sometimes she looks at you and...

00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:11.456
I swear it's like
she's reading your mind.

00:13:11.664 --> 00:13:14.123
What about you Monica?
Have you lived here long?

00:13:14.158 --> 00:13:17.164
Oh, my husband and I we bought this
place just before Rosy was born.

00:13:17.199 --> 00:13:18.409
How old is Rosy?

00:13:18.444 --> 00:13:20.358
She's six months today.

00:13:21.523 --> 00:13:24.662
It's big right? Growing like a weed.

00:13:24.697 --> 00:13:26.432
Yeah.

00:13:30.868 --> 00:13:32.874
Monica...

00:13:33.235 --> 00:13:35.000
Yeah?

00:13:36.963 --> 00:13:38.337
Just uh...

00:13:38.372 --> 00:13:40.142
Just take care of yourself, okay?

00:13:40.177 --> 00:13:42.475
Yeah, you too Sam. We'll see you around.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:42.994
Yeah.

00:13:44.729 --> 00:13:47.327
Oh, here's daddy!

00:14:51.978 --> 00:14:53.703
What are you...?

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.010
Rosy?

00:15:10.863 --> 00:15:12.775
No!

00:15:24.614 --> 00:15:26.583
A vision?

00:15:26.618 --> 00:15:28.539
Yes.

00:15:28.731 --> 00:15:31.890
I saw the Demon burning
a woman on the ceiling.

00:15:31.925 --> 00:15:34.357
Right and you think this is gonna
happen to this woman you met because...

00:15:34.392 --> 00:15:38.241
Because these things happen
exactly the way I see them.

00:15:38.276 --> 00:15:40.164
He started them as nightmares and...

00:15:40.199 --> 00:15:42.388
It started when he was awake.

00:15:42.423 --> 00:15:44.220
Yeah.

00:15:44.633 --> 00:15:47.842
It's like... I don't know,
it's like the closer I get...

00:15:47.877 --> 00:15:51.201
To anything involving the Demon
the stronger the visions get.

00:15:51.236 --> 00:15:54.295
All right, when were you
gonna tell me about this?

00:15:55.423 --> 00:15:56.842
We didn't know what it meant.

00:15:56.877 --> 00:16:01.915
All right, something like this starts happening to
your brother you pick up the phone and you call me.

00:16:02.361 --> 00:16:04.252
Call you?

00:16:05.041 --> 00:16:07.266
Are you kidding me?

00:16:08.058 --> 00:16:10.143
Dad, I called you from Lawrence.

00:16:10.178 --> 00:16:12.927
All right, Sam called
you when I was dying.

00:16:12.982 --> 00:16:16.443
I mean, getting you on the phone I got
a better chance winning the lottery.

00:16:21.798 --> 00:16:24.059
You're right.

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:30.670
Although, I'm not crazy about this new
tone of yours, you're right. I'm sorry.

00:16:30.705 --> 00:16:32.125
Look, guys. Visions or no visions.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:35.305
The fact is we know the
Demon is coming tonight.

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:38.445
And this family is going through
the same hell that we went through.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.114
No, they're not.

00:16:40.149 --> 00:16:43.510
No one is. Ever again.

00:16:49.913 --> 00:16:51.568
Hello.

00:16:51.603 --> 00:16:53.223
Sam?

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.853
Who is this?

00:16:54.888 --> 00:16:59.034
Think real hard, it'll come to you.

00:16:59.897 --> 00:17:01.728
Meg?

00:17:04.028 --> 00:17:06.311
Last time I saw you,
you fell out of a window.

00:17:06.346 --> 00:17:08.294
Yeah, thanks to you.

00:17:08.329 --> 00:17:10.650
That really hurt my feelings by the way.

00:17:10.685 --> 00:17:12.366
Just your feelings?

00:17:12.401 --> 00:17:14.969
That was a seven story drop.

00:17:15.004 --> 00:17:17.537
Let me speak to your dad.

00:17:20.013 --> 00:17:21.512
My dad?

00:17:21.547 --> 00:17:22.893
I don't know where my dad is.

00:17:22.928 --> 00:17:28.692
It's time for the grown ups to
talk, Sam. Let me speak to him, now.

00:17:37.362 --> 00:17:39.204
This is John.

00:17:39.239 --> 00:17:41.675
Howdy, John? I'm Meg.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:44.077
I'm a friend of your boys.

00:17:44.112 --> 00:17:47.768
I'm also the one who watched Jim
Murphy choke on his own blood.

00:17:50.435 --> 00:17:52.858
Still there, John boy?

00:17:52.893 --> 00:17:54.055
I'm here.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.782
That was yesterday.

00:17:55.783 --> 00:17:58.368
Today I'm in Lincoln.

00:18:00.124 --> 00:18:03.410
Visiting another old friend of yours.

00:18:03.445 --> 00:18:06.425
He wants to say hi.

00:18:06.751 --> 00:18:08.565
John, whatever they do don't...

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.121
Caleb?

00:18:11.338 --> 00:18:13.299
Caleb?

00:18:13.729 --> 00:18:15.393
You listen to me...

00:18:15.428 --> 00:18:18.762
He's got nothing to do with
anything. You let him go.

00:18:18.797 --> 00:18:21.896
We know you have the Colt, John.

00:18:22.238 --> 00:18:24.266
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:24.301 --> 00:18:25.982
Oh?

00:18:26.017 --> 00:18:27.664
Okay.

00:18:28.266 --> 00:18:30.831
So, listen to this.

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:36.513
Caleb?

00:18:36.696 --> 00:18:37.759
Caleb?

00:18:37.794 --> 00:18:39.250
You hear that?

00:18:39.285 --> 00:18:41.092
That's the sound of your friend dying.

00:18:41.127 --> 00:18:43.211
Now, let's try this again.

00:18:43.246 --> 00:18:46.545
We know you have the gun,
John. Words travel fast.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:50.617
So as far as we're concerned,
you just declared war.

00:18:50.652 --> 00:18:54.654
And this is what war looks
like. It has casualties.

00:18:55.493 --> 00:18:58.174
I'm gonna kill you, you know that?

00:18:58.209 --> 00:18:59.985
Oh, John. Please.

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:01.759
Mind your blood pressure.

00:19:01.794 --> 00:19:03.464
So, this is the thing.

00:19:03.499 --> 00:19:06.177
We're gonna keep doing what we're doing.

00:19:06.212 --> 00:19:07.930
And your friends...

00:19:07.965 --> 00:19:09.894
and anyone who has ever helped you?

00:19:09.929 --> 00:19:14.302
Gave you shelter, anyone you ever loved.

00:19:14.337 --> 00:19:18.676
They'll all die unless
you give us that gun.

00:19:22.369 --> 00:19:27.430
I'm waiting Johny. Better
answer before the buzzer.

00:19:27.883 --> 00:19:29.358
Okay.

00:19:29.393 --> 00:19:32.952
Sorry? I didn't quite get that.

00:19:32.987 --> 00:19:34.630
I said okay.

00:19:34.665 --> 00:19:37.165
I'll bring you the Colt.

00:19:37.496 --> 00:19:39.466
There's a warehouse in Lincoln.

00:19:39.501 --> 00:19:41.976
In the corner of Wellbasher and Lake.

00:19:42.011 --> 00:19:43.781
You're gonna meet me there.

00:19:43.816 --> 00:19:46.483
It's gonna take me about
a day's drive to get there.

00:19:46.518 --> 00:19:48.544
Meet me there at midnight tonight.

00:19:48.579 --> 00:19:49.283
That's impossible.

00:19:49.284 --> 00:19:52.245
I can't get there in time and I
can't just carry a gun on a plane.

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:56.257
Oh, then I guess your
friends die, don't they?

00:19:57.255 --> 00:19:59.364
If you do decide to make it...

00:19:59.399 --> 00:20:01.593
Come alone.

00:20:08.791 --> 00:20:12.139
What the hell are you looking at?

00:20:12.591 --> 00:20:14.784
So you think Meg is a demon?

00:20:14.819 --> 00:20:17.413
Either that or she's possessed by one.

00:20:17.448 --> 00:20:18.588
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:18.731 --> 00:20:18.931
What do we do?

00:20:18.766 --> 00:20:20.686
I'm going to Lincoln.

00:20:20.721 --> 00:20:21.603
What?

00:20:21.604 --> 00:20:23.481
Doesn't seem like I have a choice.

00:20:23.516 --> 00:20:27.106
If I don't go, a lot of
people die. Our friends die.

00:20:27.141 --> 00:20:29.383
Dad, the Demon is coming tonight.

00:20:29.418 --> 00:20:31.683
For Monica and her family
that gun is all we've got.

00:20:31.718 --> 00:20:33.488
You can't just hand it over.

00:20:33.523 --> 00:20:35.258
Who said about handing it over?

00:20:35.259 --> 00:20:38.128
Look, besides us and a couple of
vampires no one's really seen the gun.

00:20:38.163 --> 00:20:39.651
No one knows what it looks like.

00:20:39.686 --> 00:20:42.547
So what? You're just gonna
pick up a ringer in a pawn shop?

00:20:42.582 --> 00:20:45.029
Antique store.

00:20:45.237 --> 00:20:47.595
You're gonna hand Meg a fake
gun and hopes she doesn't notice?

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:49.685
Look, as long as it's close...

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.419
She shouldn't be able
to tell the difference.

00:20:51.454 --> 00:20:54.172
Yeah, but for how long? What
happens when she figures it out?

00:20:54.207 --> 00:20:55.394
I just...

00:20:55.429 --> 00:20:58.583
I just need to buy a
few hours, that's all.

00:20:58.618 --> 00:21:01.762
You mean for Dean and me?

00:21:04.221 --> 00:21:08.033
You want us to stay here?

00:21:08.701 --> 00:21:10.982
And kill this Demon by ourselves.

00:21:11.017 --> 00:21:13.315
No, Sam.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:16.093
I want to stop losing people we love.

00:21:16.128 --> 00:21:20.858
I want you to go to school I
want... I want Dean to have a home.

00:21:25.359 --> 00:21:29.040
I want Mary alive.

00:21:31.974 --> 00:21:34.081
It's just...

00:21:36.387 --> 00:21:40.296
I just want this to be over.

00:22:12.264 --> 00:22:14.097
Did you get it?

00:22:26.783 --> 00:22:29.418
You know this is a trap, don't you?

00:22:31.354 --> 00:22:33.093
That's why Meg wanted you to come alone.

00:22:33.128 --> 00:22:34.547
I can handle her.

00:22:34.582 --> 00:22:37.561
I have the wholed loaded.
Holy water, mandake, amu...

00:22:37.596 --> 00:22:39.057
Dad.

00:22:39.092 --> 00:22:40.519
What?

00:22:41.015 --> 00:22:42.634
Promise me something.

00:22:42.669 --> 00:22:44.759
What's that?

00:22:44.936 --> 00:22:48.976
If this doesn't go south
just get the hell out.

00:22:49.011 --> 00:22:53.284
Don't get yourself killed, all
right? You're no good to us dead.

00:22:55.991 --> 00:22:58.871
Same goes for you.

00:22:59.947 --> 00:23:02.316
All right, listen to me.

00:23:03.082 --> 00:23:06.659
They made the bullets
special for this Colt.

00:23:06.694 --> 00:23:08.947
Only four of them left.

00:23:08.982 --> 00:23:12.624
Without them, this gun is useless.

00:23:14.309 --> 00:23:16.399
You make every shot count.

00:23:16.434 --> 00:23:17.914
Yes, sir.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:23.953
I've been waiting a
long time for this fight.

00:23:23.988 --> 00:23:28.206
Now it's here and I'm
not gonna be in it.

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:32.134
It's up to you boys now.

00:23:34.044 --> 00:23:36.589
It's your fight. You finish this.

00:23:36.624 --> 00:23:38.773
You finished what I started.

00:23:38.808 --> 00:23:41.169
You understand?

00:24:01.612 --> 00:24:04.309
We'll see you soon dad.

00:24:08.458 --> 00:24:10.155
I'll see you later.

00:24:35.133 --> 00:24:37.168
Later...

00:25:59.993 --> 00:26:02.144
Maybe we can tell them
there's a gas leak.

00:26:02.179 --> 00:26:04.827
Might get them out of
the house for a few hours.

00:26:04.862 --> 00:26:08.386
How many times did that work for us?

00:26:08.586 --> 00:26:10.137
Yeah.

00:26:13.367 --> 00:26:17.078
Could always tell them the truth.

00:26:18.781 --> 00:26:19.991
Na...

00:26:20.026 --> 00:26:21.202
I know.

00:26:21.203 --> 00:26:24.279
I know, I know, I just...

00:26:24.314 --> 00:26:26.218
What's to become of these people?

00:26:26.253 --> 00:26:28.684
Sam, we only got one move
and you know it, all right?

00:26:28.719 --> 00:26:31.116
We got to wait for that Demon
to show itself and then...

00:26:31.151 --> 00:26:34.162
We get it before it gets them.

00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:41.212
I wonder what dad's doing.

00:26:43.081 --> 00:26:47.053
I would feel a lot better if
we were there backing him up.

00:26:49.340 --> 00:26:53.450
I would feel a lot better
if he was here backing us up.

00:28:29.412 --> 00:28:31.668
This is what we have.

00:28:32.170 --> 00:28:33.990
What?

00:28:34.510 --> 00:28:38.027
After all those years
we're finally here.

00:28:38.062 --> 00:28:40.680
It doesn't seem real.

00:28:41.553 --> 00:28:45.379
We just got to keep our heads
and do our job like always.

00:28:45.414 --> 00:28:48.710
Yeah, but this isn't like always.

00:28:51.491 --> 00:28:53.581
True.

00:28:55.197 --> 00:28:57.522
Dean, uh...

00:29:00.226 --> 00:29:02.668
I want to thank you.

00:29:03.723 --> 00:29:06.297
For what?

00:29:08.355 --> 00:29:10.893
For everything.

00:29:10.928 --> 00:29:13.102
You've always led my back you know.

00:29:13.137 --> 00:29:17.449
Even when I can't count on anyone
I could always count on you.

00:29:17.484 --> 00:29:19.538
And now...

00:29:19.893 --> 00:29:22.591
I don't know, I just
want to let you know.

00:29:22.626 --> 00:29:23.900
Just incase.

00:29:23.935 --> 00:29:26.365
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Are you kidding me?

00:29:26.400 --> 00:29:27.417
What?

00:29:27.452 --> 00:29:29.565
Don't say just incase
something happens to you.

00:29:29.600 --> 00:29:31.679
I don't want to hear
that freaking speech man.

00:29:31.714 --> 00:29:33.865
Nobody is dying tonight.

00:29:33.900 --> 00:29:36.973
Not us, not that family, nobody.

00:29:37.574 --> 00:29:39.825
Except that Demon.

00:29:39.860 --> 00:29:44.752
That evil son of a bitch ain't getting
any older than tonight. You understand me?

00:29:56.007 --> 00:29:58.199
John. You made it.

00:29:58.234 --> 00:30:00.356
Too bad really.

00:30:00.391 --> 00:30:02.819
I was hoping to kill
more of your friends.

00:30:02.854 --> 00:30:05.046
Sorry to disappoint.

00:30:05.081 --> 00:30:08.752
I can see where your
boys get their good looks.

00:30:08.787 --> 00:30:14.820
I must admit, considering what they
say about you I thought you'd be taller.

00:30:17.301 --> 00:30:20.073
Well, aren't you the chatty one?

00:30:20.108 --> 00:30:22.845
You want to get to business?

00:30:23.486 --> 00:30:25.189
Fine.

00:30:25.902 --> 00:30:27.841
Why don't you hand over the gun?

00:30:27.876 --> 00:30:30.843
If I give you the gun,
how do I get out of here?

00:30:30.878 --> 00:30:34.924
If you're as good as they say you are,
I'm sure you'll figure something out.

00:30:34.959 --> 00:30:36.868
Maybe I'll just shoot you.

00:30:36.903 --> 00:30:39.500
You want to shoot me, baby? Go ahead.

00:30:39.535 --> 00:30:44.577
It won't end anything.
There's more where I came from.

00:30:48.745 --> 00:30:50.311
Who the hell's that?

00:30:50.346 --> 00:30:54.685
He's not as nearly as much fun
as I am, I can tell you that.

00:30:54.720 --> 00:30:58.536
So, I suggest you give us the gun.

00:31:04.699 --> 00:31:07.036
Now!

00:31:17.294 --> 00:31:19.482
This is the Colt?

00:31:24.986 --> 00:31:27.522
What do you think?

00:31:48.819 --> 00:31:51.172
You shot me!

00:31:51.756 --> 00:31:55.339
I can't believe you just shot me!

00:31:56.571 --> 00:31:58.859
It's a fake!

00:32:08.725 --> 00:32:10.232
You're dead John.

00:32:10.267 --> 00:32:11.705
You're boys are dead.

00:32:11.740 --> 00:32:14.716
I never used the gun. How can
I know it would never work?

00:32:14.751 --> 00:32:17.693
I'm so not in the mood for
this. I've just been shot!

00:32:17.728 --> 00:32:20.621
Well I guess you're
lucky the gun wasn't real.

00:32:20.656 --> 00:32:22.414
That's funny, John.

00:32:22.449 --> 00:32:27.853
We're gonna strip the skin from
your bones but that was funny.

00:33:12.258 --> 00:33:14.811
Holy water, John.

00:33:14.846 --> 00:33:17.707
Real cute.

00:33:27.910 --> 00:33:30.491
Dad's not answering.

00:33:33.466 --> 00:33:35.383
Maybe Meg was late.

00:33:35.418 --> 00:33:37.006
Maybe the reception is bad.

00:33:37.041 --> 00:33:38.348
Yeah, well...

00:33:43.763 --> 00:33:45.965
Dean, wait.

00:33:46.849 --> 00:33:48.531
Listen.

00:34:11.559 --> 00:34:13.701
It's coming.

00:34:21.529 --> 00:34:23.082
Damn it.

00:34:51.019 --> 00:34:52.752
Get out of my house!

00:34:54.038 --> 00:34:55.772
Get out of my house!

00:34:57.732 --> 00:34:58.811
Mr. Hold, please.

00:34:58.846 --> 00:34:59.743
Be quite and listen to me.

00:34:59.744 --> 00:35:01.960
Be quite and listen to me.
We are trying to help you.

00:35:01.995 --> 00:35:02.964
Charlie?

00:35:02.999 --> 00:35:03.933
Okay?

00:35:03.934 --> 00:35:05.071
Everything okay down there?

00:35:05.106 --> 00:35:06.080
Monica, get the baby!

00:35:06.081 --> 00:35:07.257
Don't go over there!

00:35:07.292 --> 00:35:08.433
You stay away from her!

00:35:14.463 --> 00:35:16.809
What are you..

00:35:31.575 --> 00:35:33.008
Where the hell did it go?

00:35:33.043 --> 00:35:33.543
My baby!

00:35:33.578 --> 00:35:35.050
No, hey wait.

00:35:35.051 --> 00:35:36.990
Get her out of here, I got it.

00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:38.469
Come on.

00:35:38.504 --> 00:35:39.463
My baby!

00:35:39.498 --> 00:35:40.529
Dean's got her.

00:36:36.888 --> 00:36:38.873
You get away from my family!

00:36:38.908 --> 00:36:40.858
Charlie, don't. They saved us.

00:36:40.893 --> 00:36:42.505
They saved us...

00:36:50.380 --> 00:36:52.231
Thank you.

00:36:56.317 --> 00:36:57.983
It's still in there.

00:36:58.263 --> 00:36:59.378
Sam, Sam. No!

00:36:59.413 --> 00:37:00.754
Dean, let me go. It's still in there!

00:37:00.789 --> 00:37:02.095
It's burning to the
ground. It's suicide!

00:37:02.130 --> 00:37:02.964
I don't care!

00:37:02.999 --> 00:37:04.293
I do!

00:37:20.277 --> 00:37:24.139
Come on, dad. Answer
your phone, damn it!

00:37:27.744 --> 00:37:30.239
Something's wrong.

00:37:32.344 --> 00:37:34.516
You hear me? Something's happened.

00:37:34.551 --> 00:37:36.688
If you had just let me go in there...

00:37:36.723 --> 00:37:39.928
I could have ended all this.

00:37:39.963 --> 00:37:41.342
Sam...

00:37:41.377 --> 00:37:44.477
The only thing you
would end was your life.

00:37:45.155 --> 00:37:47.512
You don't know that.

00:37:47.547 --> 00:37:51.164
So what? You're willing to
sacrifice yourself? Is that it?

00:37:51.673 --> 00:37:53.915
Yeah. Yeah, you're damn right I am.

00:37:53.950 --> 00:37:56.157
Yeah, well that's not gonna
happen. Not as long as I'm around.

00:37:56.192 --> 00:37:57.701
What the hell are you
talking about Dean?

00:37:57.736 --> 00:38:00.467
We've been searching for
this Demon our whole lives.

00:38:00.502 --> 00:38:02.108
It's the only thing
we've ever cared about.

00:38:02.143 --> 00:38:04.917
Sam, I want to waste it. I do, okay?

00:38:04.952 --> 00:38:06.911
But it's not worth dying over?

00:38:06.946 --> 00:38:07.465
What?

00:38:07.500 --> 00:38:08.815
I mean it.

00:38:08.816 --> 00:38:12.285
If hunting this Demon means
you getting yourself killed.

00:38:12.320 --> 00:38:14.667
Then I hope we never
find the damn thing.

00:38:14.702 --> 00:38:17.683
That thing killed Jess.

00:38:18.585 --> 00:38:21.345
That thing killed mom.

00:38:21.813 --> 00:38:24.728
You said yourself once.

00:38:24.879 --> 00:38:27.871
That no matter what we do they're gone

00:38:27.906 --> 00:38:30.313
and they're never coming back.

00:38:30.771 --> 00:38:33.534
Don't just say that! Don't you!

00:38:33.569 --> 00:38:36.297
After all this, don't you say that.

00:38:37.879 --> 00:38:41.480
Sam, look.

00:38:41.515 --> 00:38:44.332
The three of us...

00:38:44.535 --> 00:38:47.331
That's all we have.

00:38:48.837 --> 00:38:51.861
It's all I have.

00:38:55.084 --> 00:38:59.342
Sometimes I feel like I'm
barely holding it together, man.

00:39:00.204 --> 00:39:03.096
Without you and dad...

00:39:04.070 --> 00:39:06.139
Dad...

00:39:11.225 --> 00:39:13.601
He should have called by now.

00:39:13.636 --> 00:39:16.101
Try again.

00:39:32.627 --> 00:39:36.439
You boys really screwed up this time.

00:39:39.308 --> 00:39:41.658
Where is he?

00:39:41.838 --> 00:39:45.090
You're never gonna
see your father again.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.250
